#question(title: [Odd functions])[
  #set text(size: 13pt)

  #slide-block(title: [Theorem])[
    Let $f$ be a continuous function. Let
    $a > 0$. IF $f$ is odd, THEN
    $
      integral_(-a)^a f(x) d x = 0
    $
  ]

  + Write down the definition of “odd
    function".
  + Draw a picture to interpret the theorem
    geometrically.
  + Prove the theorem!

     #emph[Hint:] Write the integral as sum
     of two pieces. Use a substitution to
     show that one of the two pieces equals
     minus the other.
]
